# Wayfarer loop agent session

Use when the user asks to run the **controller loop**, `/loop`, or when a Cursor Automation fires on the Wayfarer schedule.

## Before coding

1. Run `bash scripts/loop-state.sh` and follow the `action` field.
2. Read `docs/agents/autonomous-workflow.md` and `docs/agents/issue-tracker.md`.
3. Load `.agents/skills/tdd/SKILL.md` for implementation slices.

## Session rules

- **Do not ask which issue to pick** — the loop state machine decides.
- **WIP=1** — only the claimed `in-progress` issue.
- On `claim_new`: `bash scripts/claim-issue.sh <n> <branch>` before editing code.
- On `repair`: fix the same branch/PR from the trusted FAIL comment whose marker matches the current head.
- On `wait_evaluator` or `idle`: stop without coding.

## Verification

| Change type | Command |
| --- | --- |
| Models / utils only | `make test` |
| UI, routing, persistence, E2E | `make check` |

## PR

- End with **PR ready for evaluator** — not "done".
- Body: `Closes #<n>`, acceptance criteria, verification section.

## Out of scope

- Picking a second issue while WIP is occupied
- Self-certifying evaluator PASS
- Merging PRs (human review only)
